  "ai_overview": {
    "text_blocks": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "Pulmonary arterial hypertension (PAH) causes high blood pressure in the lung arteries, leading to symptoms that typically develop slowly over time as the right side of the heart works harder to pump blood.",
        "snippet_highlighted_words": [
          "high blood pressure in the lung arteries"
        ],
        "reference_indexes": [
          0,
          1,
          2,
          3,
          4
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Common Symptoms"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Shortness of breath (dyspnea): Usually starts during physical activity or exercise, but can eventually occur even while resting in advanced stages."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Fatigue and weakness: Feeling exceptionally tired or lacking the energy for normal daily tasks."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Chest pain or pressure: Caused by the extra strain placed on the heart muscle."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Dizziness or lightheadedness: Frequently triggered by exertion."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Fainting (syncope): Passing out during physical activity due to drops in blood pressure or inadequate blood flow."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Heart palpitations: Sensations of a racing, pounding, or skipping heartbeat."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Swelling (edema): Fluid buildup causing swelling in the ankles, legs, feet, or abdomen."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Cyanosis: A bluish or grayish tint to the lips, skin, or fingers caused by low oxygen levels."
          }
        ],
        "reference_indexes": [
          2,
          3,
          4,
          5,
          6,
          7,
          8,
          9
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Progression and Advanced Signs"
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "Symptoms often mimic other common heart and lung conditions early on, which can delay diagnosis. As the condition progresses and impacts right heart function, individuals may experience a chronic cough, an enlarged liver, or hoarseness from nerve compression in the chest. You can learn more from UCHealth or CheckRare .",
        "snippet_links": [
          {
            "text": "UCHealth",
            "link": "https://www.uchealth.org/diseases-conditions/pulmonary-hypertension/"
          },
          {
            "text": "CheckRare",
            "link": "https://checkrare.com/pulmonary-arterial-hypertension/"
          }
        ],
        "reference_indexes": [
          0,
          3,
          7,
          10
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "If you or someone you know is experiencing these symptoms, let me know:"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Are they worsening or interfering with daily activities?"
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Is there a family history of pulmonary or heart conditions?"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "I can help outline what diagnostic tests doctors typically use to evaluate PAH."
      }
